  Discovery listed 6,621 cases in each configuration. Positive-view-Z and both transferred PBR
  restoration tests passed 3/3 in each configuration; the original exact source-restoration and
  .01 indirect replacement-restoration tolerances were preserved alongside PBR numerical oracles.
  Independent review is clean after those oracle transfers, preservation of all five cloud
  diagnostic profiles, and correction of native-inventory ownership wording.
  The full Debug run passed 6,620 with zero failures and seven skips in 732.960s, excluding builds.
  Six skips match baseline; the additional ProfilerEventSource EventListener skip is unrelated to
  the reduction and is not a saving. The old snapshot-startup timeout did not recur; no fix is claimed.
  There are 395 fewer runtime rows: 396 old IDs removed and one positive-view-Z Fact ID added.
  The 823 changed-suite cases matched the intended selections. All 16 scoped source hashes,
  both test DLLs and per-configuration shader binaries remained stable during their checks;
  all 909 test SPIR-V modules per configuration match the original full-run baseline.
  These single sequential samples retain caches and do not establish a stable speedup.
  Receipts: ../TestResults/TestRuntimeOptimizations/five-minute-investigation/representative-candidate/
